Ladybird now takes a replaced box’s min-content block size from its
preferred aspect ratio, so an image with “aspect-ratio: 4 / 3” keeps
the height its width gives as its automatic minimum. Run in Chrome
157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5, all three
engines keep it at 225px.

Blink’s FlexLayoutAlgorithm::ConstructAndAppendFlexItems() measures the
content size suggestion of a replaced item with ComputeReplacedSize(),
and BlockNode::GetReplacedAspectRatio() prefers the CSS aspect ratio.
WebKit’s FlexFormattingContext::computeContentBasedMinMainSize() takes
it from the cross size through preferredAspectRatioForFlexItem(), which
also prefers the CSS ratio. Gecko’s ResolveAutoFlexBasisAndMinSize()
measures it with MeasureFlexItemContentBSize(), and nsIFrame::
GetAspectRatio() prefers the CSS ratio.
